The first is a list of 1, 2, 3, 2, and 1.
The second is a list of 3, 2, 1, 4, and 7.
The rowsend is the last position of first.
The columnsend is the last position of second.
The rows is rowsend plus 1.
The columns is columnsend plus 1.
The width is columns plus 1.
The size is (rows plus 1) times width.
The table is a list of size zeros.
The best is 0.
For every firstspot from 1 to rows.
For every secondspot from 1 to columns.
The index is firstspot times width plus secondspot.
If item (firstspot minus 1) of first is item (secondspot minus 1) of second, set item index of table to item (index minus width minus 1) of table plus 1.
If item index of table is more than best, set best to item index of table.

Show best.

